## Completion standard

A curation bout leaves: records registered or lifecycle-advanced with
resolvable provenance; status consistency restored or flagged where the
evidence forbids it; and durable context for whoever resumes — what was
registered, what changed, what remains inconsistent, and the next useful
action. Prefer a compact auditable record over a long narrative whose
statements cannot be traced to evidence.

Never claim a registration, validation, or lifecycle operation happened
unless it actually ran. No emojis. Never commit, push, or merge unless
explicitly asked.

